WEBVTT

NOTE Timed to the recorded help-desk video (media/video/helpdesk.mp4).

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.900
Welcome back to the Normalcy Files.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.200
We’ll be taking a trip through the Roaring Twenties,

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.800
a decade of jazz, dancing, and exciting new trends,

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.300
a time of incredible creativity, cultural change,

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.600
and people fighting to be heard,

6
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.200
and the decade of questions about inequality, political scandals,

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.900
and whether America was really as prosperous as it seemed to be.

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.100
So what was life really like in the 1920s?

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.600
And did President Harding’s promise of a return to normalcy actually work?

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.200
That’s where you come in.

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.500
Explore the exhibits and discover the stories behind the artifacts.

12
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.300
Use WASD or the arrow keys to move.

13
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.800
See something sparkling? Use E or Space to investigate.

14
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.600
Find gold stars, play mini-games, and press N to hear the room’s narration.

15
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.900
Need help finding your way? Press M for the map and follow the gold arrow.

16
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.200
Visit all six exhibits, check your sources in the Library,

17
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.200
and head down to the Courthouse to make your final judgment.

18
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.900
The past is full of surprises, and the truth is waiting to be discovered.

19
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.200
Let’s open the files!

